# Vulnerabilities intentionally suppressed from the CI scan gate.
# Each entry must have a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore here -
# see .claude/MEMORY.md ("Known wont-fix CVEs") for the full write-up.

# tesseract-ocr 5.5.2-r0 (Alpine). No fixed release exists anywhere upstream
# as of 2026-09 (checked Alpine edge: still 5.5.3-r0, which the CVEs say is
# also affected) - these are not "upgrade available" findings.
# Both require Tesseract to load an attacker-crafted .traineddata model file
# to trigger (stack/heap overflow while parsing NORMPROTO / NT_SOFTMAX
# layers). This gateway only ever loads the single trusted eng.traineddata
# shipped by Alpine's tesseract-ocr-data-eng package - ocr.py/ocr_api.py
# never accept a user-supplied model path or let request input choose which
# .traineddata loads. Not reachable via the /v1/ocr endpoint.
CVE-2026-88047
CVE-2026-88048

# Same package, same trigger (crafted .traineddata model) and same
# reasoning as above: out-of-bounds reads/writes while parsing a model's
# GenericVector counts (88051), unicharset (88052) and inttemp (88053)
# sections. Fixed on upstream main (56e09ca1, 2d04d640, 8b057468) but
# unreleased; upstream advisories target 5.5.4. Remove all tesseract
# entries once tesseract-ocr >= 5.5.4 is packaged in Alpine.
CVE-2026-88051
CVE-2026-88052
CVE-2026-88053

# zlib 1.3.2-r0 (Alpine). Heap overflow in gz_vacate() reached only via the
# gzFile API: gzprintf()/gzvprintf() after a non-blocking gzwrite() stall.
# Fixed on upstream develop (df84af25) but unreleased; Alpine edge is still
# 1.3.2-r0. No binary or library in this image references
# gzprintf/gzvprintf/gzwrite (only libz.so itself) - Python, Pillow, Poppler,
# Tesseract, Leptonica and libtiff use only in-memory inflate/deflate - and
# the gateway code imports neither zlib nor gzip. Remove once zlib > 1.3.2
# is packaged in Alpine.
CVE-2026-85091
